    {
      "skill_id": "pt-b2-026",
      "title": "Formal clitic placement: ênclise, próclise and auxiliaries",
      "explanation": "The formal written norm places the pronoun by rule. A clause may not begin with an unstressed pronoun, so the pronoun follows the verb with a hyphen (ênclise): disse-me a verdade, diga-me, explicou-lhe a lição. After a negative, a conjunction or relative such as que and quando, certain adverbs (já, sempre, nunca) and indefinite pronouns (todos, ninguém), the pronoun goes before the verb (próclise): não me disse, que o viu, já o vi, todos a conhecem. With ter or haver plus a participle the pronoun attaches to the auxiliary and never to the participle: tenho-o visto, não o tinha visto. Do not hyphenate after a participle (tenho visto-o is wrong) and do not start a clause with me, te or lhe.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "pt": "Disse-me a verdade.",
          "en": "He told me the truth."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Não me disse a verdade.",
          "en": "He did not tell me the truth."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Tenho-o visto.",
          "en": "I have seen him."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["COE-CV20"],
