    {
      "skill_id": "pt-b2-027",
      "title": "Mesóclise: the pronoun inside the future and the conditional",
      "explanation": "In the futuro do presente and the futuro do pretérito, the formal norm does not allow the pronoun after the verb, so a clause that begins with the verb puts the pronoun inside it: dar-lhe-ei, dir-te-ia, enviá-lo-emos. The infinitive stays whole and the future or conditional ending follows it, with a hyphen on each side of the pronoun. Verbs ending in -r lose the r before o, a, os and as (enviar plus o gives enviá-lo). The same attractors that call for próclise still apply: não lhe darei, nunca te diria. Do not write the pronoun after a future verb (darei-lhe is wrong in formal writing) or before it at the start of a clause (lhe darei is wrong).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "pt": "Dar-lhe-ei a resposta amanhã.",
          "en": "I will give him the answer tomorrow."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Dir-te-ia a verdade.",
          "en": "I would tell you the truth."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Enviá-lo-emos amanhã.",
          "en": "We will send it tomorrow."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["COE-CV20"],
