    {
      "skill_id": "pt-b2-029",
      "title": "Verb government in formal Portuguese",
      "explanation": "Many verbs require a specific preposition in the formal norm, and the preposition changes with the sense. Assistir a means to watch or attend (assisti ao filme). Preferir takes a (prefiro café a chá, not do que). Obedecer and desobedecer take a (obedecer às regras). Aspirar a means to aim for (aspira a um cargo), and visar a means to aim at (visa a vencer). Lembrar-se and esquecer-se take de (lembra-se do nome); consistir takes em; implicar takes no preposition (implica mudanças). Do not drop the preposition the verb requires (assisti o filme is wrong in formal writing) and do not add one it forbids.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "pt": "Assisti ao filme novo.",
          "en": "I watched the new film."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Prefiro café a chá.",
          "en": "I prefer coffee to tea."
        },
        {
          "pt": "Os alunos devem obedecer às regras.",
          "en": "Students must obey the rules."
        }
      ],
      "references": ["COE-CV20"],
