      "skill_id": "pt-b2-030",
      "title": "Crase: a, à and há",
      "explanation": "Crase is the contraction of the preposition a with the article a or as, or with the initial a of aquele, aquela and aquilo: vou à escola, entreguei o relatório à diretora, ela chegou às oito, referi-me àquela reunião. It is written with the grave accent. Use it when the verb or noun requires a and the following word accepts a feminine article. Do not use it before masculine words, verbs, most pronouns or place names that take no article (vou a Lisboa, but vou à Bahia). The set phrases à tarde, à noite and à medida que carry crase. Há with an accent is the verb haver and means ago or there is (cheguei há dois dias); do not confuse it with a (cheguei a Lisboa).",
